WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.834
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:05.367
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:08.934
♪♪

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:11.701
We are right in the middle
of the holiday season,

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:14.467
and I saw that Instacart
is now offering

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:17.167
same-day delivery
for Christmas trees.

00:00:17.167 --> 00:00:19.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.300
So remember to tip,
because your delivery guy

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.834
definitely has an ax.

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:26.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:27.868
Yeah, wow.

00:00:27.868 --> 00:00:31.300
Of course, it's Instacart, so
get ready for a text that says,

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.334
"They're out of Christmas trees.

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:33.467
Is Pepsi okay?"

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:36.434
And you go, "Pepsi?
That's not even --"

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:40.200
Yep, Christmas trees
on Instacart.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.000
It's a beautiful
new family tradition

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.133
of gathering around papa
until he swipes right

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.400
on the perfect balsam fir.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.968
"Dad's getting his phone out.
Come on, let's gather up."

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:53.167
I don't want someone else
picking out my Christmas tree.

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:55.067
I don't even like someone else
picking out my cantaloupe.

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:56.400
I was like, "Oh.
You thought that was ripe?

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.667
Didn't you knock on it?"

00:00:58.667 --> 00:00:59.667
Is that what you do with
a cantaloupe?

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:01.033
Do you knock on it?

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.467
-You got to thwap the end.
You smell it. You know.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:03.534
-Certain things I just knock on

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:05.601
and think I know
what I'm talking about.

00:01:05.601 --> 00:01:07.801
Do you knock on a pineapple?
That does nothing.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.400
You peel the leaf of
a pineapple.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:10.534
-You pull the leaf.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:12.033
-Watermelon I knock on,
of course.

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.701
That goes without saying.
-Knock on wood.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.300
-I knock on watermelons
I don't even buy.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.601
I just go up and go,
"Hey, what's up?"

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:18.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:20.434
-Fill it with vodka.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:21.767
Did you guys see this?

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:24.567
New York just passed a law that
makes all gift cards

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:27.868
purchased in the state
valid for at least nine years.

00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:29.133
-Ooh!

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.033
-You know you got someone
the perfect gift card

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:34.100
when it takes them 8 1/2 years
to use it.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.934
"Well, you like
Home Depot, so..."

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.334
8 1/2 -- Yeah.

00:01:38.334 --> 00:01:40.467
They're good for nine years,
although I'm not quite sure

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.968
what to do with a valid gift
card from Borders Bookstore.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:44.167
What am I doing?
What am I doing?

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.801
Find me a Borders.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:47.100
Let's get to some news.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.901
Due to a rise in
COVID, RSV, and flu cases,

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:52.534
New York City health officials
issued an advisory

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:54.701
urging people
to wear masks again.

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:56.067
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:57.734
I think they're getting
tired of these announcements,

00:01:57.734 --> 00:01:59.501
'cause this one felt a little
more casual than the rest.

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:00.567
Take a look at this.

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:04.868
That's...
-Wow.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.801
-That was fast.
♪♪

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:08.367
That's it?

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:13.868
That was fast.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:15.534
That's right -- New York City
is experiencing

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.901
high levels of
COVID, flu, and RSV,

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:20.701
and health officials are
calling it a "tridemic."

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:23.067
-Aw, come on, man.
We can do better than that.

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:24.601
-What's that, Tariq?

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:27.501
-I said we can come up with
a better name than a "tridemic."

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:28.501
That's so clunky.

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:29.701
-Yeah, you're right.

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:31.033
"Tridemic" doesn't even
rhyme with anything.

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:32.067
What are you thinking?

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:33.868
-Um, the three-sles.

00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:36.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:38.534
-That's good.

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:40.567
Scarlet three-ver.

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:43.534
-Uh...hepa-thri-tis.

00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:46.767
-Gono-three-a.

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:50.467
-The thrice-capades.

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:51.868
-The thrice is right.

00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:53.501
-Trip-slip.

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:54.734
-Fuzzy triple.

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:56.767
-Mm...

00:02:56.767 --> 00:02:59.400
uh, "Three Strains and a Baby."

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.534
-"Three Strains and a Rabies."

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:02.033
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:04.901
-Once, twice, three
types of achy.

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:07.367
-The Tri Guys.

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:09.634
-We can just call it
"Three's Company."

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:12.133
-How about "All I Want for
Christmas is Achoo"?

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:15.067
-Rocking around
a Christmas three.

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:17.501
-Oh. The tres race.

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:19.634
-Ooh! The tres force.

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:21.067
-Left without a tres.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:25.968
-All aboard the flu-flu strain
choo-choo train.

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:28.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:30.067
-That's it.

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:32.400
That's the one. That's it.
Tariq Trotter got it right.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.634
[ Dinging ]
That's it, buddy.

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:35.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:41.167
Well, guys,
Elon Musk is still on his

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:43.200
"trying to make
people upset" tour.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.467
And Elon is being slammed
for a tweet

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:48.934
he posted yesterday that said...

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:56.434
Fauci was like, "Yep,
much like a Tesla battery,

00:03:56.434 --> 00:03:57.734
Elon's on fire."

00:03:57.734 --> 00:03:59.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:01.767
Yeah. You could tell Fauci
wasn't having it

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:03.701
because he wrote back,
"Congrats on making Twitter

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:06.067
the Johnson &amp; Johnson vaccine
of social media."

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:11.267
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:12.567
Thank you.

00:04:12.567 --> 00:04:14.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:17.100
Meanwhile, Elon also said that
Twitter's character limit

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:21.734
for tweets is going to increase
from 280 to 4,000.

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:25.033
People are like,
"4,000 characters?

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:27.667
At that point, I may as well get
my news from the news."

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.767
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:32.033
Switching gears,
King Charles just released

00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:35.300
the first royal
Christmas card of his reign.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.567
Ready for it? Here it is.

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:40.100
"Wishing you a very happy
Christmas and New Year."

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.834
It has the same
emotional feeling

00:04:41.834 --> 00:04:43.501
as a holiday card
from your dentist.

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:45.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.300
"I can see through this."

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.567
Seriously, the love and emotion
just flows from that guy's pen.

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:52.601
Are there budget cuts
at Buckingham Palace?

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:54.934
Is that --
Is Elon firing everyone

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:57.234
in the card division over there?

00:04:57.234 --> 00:04:58.434
Well, here's some big news.

00:04:58.434 --> 00:05:00.200
The other day, a lot of people
were surprised to

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:04.234
see Ben Affleck getting coffee
at Starbucks.

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:07.901
-Oh!
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:10.067
-Ben Affleck was
drinking Starbucks,

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:11.701
and it didn't take long for
Dunkin' to respond.

00:05:11.701 --> 00:05:12.734
Watch this.

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:14.467
-Well, well.

00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:18.734
You think you're better than us,
Benedict Affleck?

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:21.000
You think you're wicked smart
going to Starbucks,

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.801
sipping $6 drinks like
the freaking King of England?

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:26.434
Enjoy your foam in a dome,
you L.A. jabron.

00:05:26.434 --> 00:05:27.834
Just go ahead and go.

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:29.934
Tom Brady left us,
and we're fine.

00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:33.534
We still got Matt Damon
and a half-dozen Wahlbergs.

00:05:33.534 --> 00:05:34.801
We'll bounce back,

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:37.567
even if we feel the way
Bill Belichick looks.

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:43.868
-Oh! That's so sad. Wow.

00:05:43.868 --> 00:05:45.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:49.100
♪♪

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.801
Guys, we are right in the middle
of the holiday season.

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:53.234
Are you excited?

00:05:53.234 --> 00:05:56.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.133
According to a survey,
during the holidays,

00:05:58.133 --> 00:06:01.734
most dog owners
buy a gift for their pet.

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:03.567
Yeah.
And then there's the people

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:05.968
that are too lazy to shop
and just give their dog cash.

00:06:05.968 --> 00:06:08.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.100
Buying a gift for a dog
is stressful.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.567
I mean, seriously,
there's nothing more depressing

00:06:11.567 --> 00:06:13.067
than watching your dog
open a present

00:06:13.067 --> 00:06:14.701
then fake wagging his tail.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.701 --> 00:06:17.467
You go, "Okay.
He didn't like it. Okay."

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:19.367
Let's get to some news.
Today, President Biden

00:06:19.367 --> 00:06:21.100
hosted a ceremony
on the South Lawn

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:23.601
to sign a bill that mandates
federal recognition

00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:25.000
for same-sex marriages.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:29.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:32.167
Yeah.

00:06:32.167 --> 00:06:34.167
When he heard,
Mike Pence was like,

00:06:34.167 --> 00:06:36.133
"Barkeep, give me a shot
of whole milk."

00:06:36.133 --> 00:06:38.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.534
"Just leave the whole carton."

00:06:39.534 --> 00:06:40.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:42.367
Yeah, the bill protects
all marriages.

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:43.667
Unless you're
one of those couples

00:06:43.667 --> 00:06:45.834
who feed each other in public.
Then you're on your own.

00:06:45.834 --> 00:06:48.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:51.133
I read that Ivanka Trump
and Jared Kushner

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:53.267
cut ties
with former president Trump

00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:56.701
because he's "losing value"
and they don't need him anymore.

00:06:56.701 --> 00:06:59.133
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:00.467
Trump's not even upset.

00:07:00.467 --> 00:07:02.801
He's like, "The student
has become the master."

00:07:02.801 --> 00:07:04.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.701 --> 00:07:06.367
Things are so rough
in the Trump family,

00:07:06.367 --> 00:07:08.100
even the royal family's like,
"Yikes."

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:09.634
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.634 --> 00:07:10.834
Did you guys see this today?

00:07:10.834 --> 00:07:13.167
A bipartisan group of lawmakers
announced a bill

00:07:13.167 --> 00:07:15.968
that would ban TikTok
in the U.S.

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:18.200
-[ Person whistles ]

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.334
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.334 --> 00:07:22.767
Right now, gen Z is like,
"We ride at dawn."

00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:27.734
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.734 --> 00:07:30.801
Critics of TikTok worry that the
app is giving American secrets

00:07:30.801 --> 00:07:32.667
to the Chinese government.

00:07:32.667 --> 00:07:34.801
Yeah, pretty scary.
Apparently, China has already

00:07:34.801 --> 00:07:36.534
mastered the "Wednesday" dance.

00:07:36.534 --> 00:07:40.901
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.901 --> 00:07:43.667
Meanwhile, get this,
a TikTok-famous plastic surgeon

00:07:43.667 --> 00:07:45.868
just had her
medical license suspended

00:07:45.868 --> 00:07:49.334
after she was accused
of botched surgeries.

00:07:49.334 --> 00:07:52.167
See, that's why I only use
YouTube-famous plastic surgeons.

00:07:52.167 --> 00:07:53.868
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.868 --> 00:07:55.100
When asked for a comment,
she said,

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.701
"Look, I don't see them
as botched surgeries.

00:07:56.701 --> 00:07:58.334
I look at them as cool filters."

00:07:58.334 --> 00:07:59.634
[ Laughter ]

00:07:59.634 --> 00:08:02.067
Well, guys, New York City
is experiencing high levels

00:08:02.067 --> 00:08:05.067
of COVID, flu, and RSV
in what health officials

00:08:05.067 --> 00:08:07.701
are calling a "tridemic."

00:08:07.701 --> 00:08:09.634
And Pfizer is promoting
a new booster shot

00:08:09.634 --> 00:08:11.634
to protect against it.
Check this out.

00:08:11.634 --> 00:08:14.100
-As cases continue to rise,
experts recommend

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:18.000
getting the latest boosters
for COVID, the flu, and RSV.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.601
But as the holidays approach,
we might not all have time

00:08:20.601 --> 00:08:21.934
for multiple appointments.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:23.234
That's why we're introducing

00:08:23.234 --> 00:08:24.734
The Destroyer.

00:08:24.734 --> 00:08:26.834
Just one quick jab,
and you're protected from...

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:44.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:44.901 --> 00:08:47.767
♪♪

00:08:47.767 --> 00:08:51.801
-Wow, indeed!
-Wow!

00:08:51.801 --> 00:08:55.400
Multiple injections.
Oh, my goodness.

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:56.901
Firecrotch, unbelievable.

00:08:56.901 --> 00:08:59.100
[ Laughter ]

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.200
Hey, I want to say
happy birthday to Bob Barker

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:02.801
who just turned 99!

00:09:02.801 --> 00:09:04.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:04.767 --> 00:09:08.334
We love you, Bob.

00:09:08.334 --> 00:09:10.033
You could tell he hosted
"The Price is Right"

00:09:10.033 --> 00:09:11.667
'cause that's the closest
you can come to 100

00:09:11.667 --> 00:09:12.734
without going over.

00:09:12.734 --> 00:09:15.734
[ Laughter ]

00:09:15.734 --> 00:09:17.701
Switching gears,
Uber Eats released

00:09:17.701 --> 00:09:19.634
its annual Cravings Report,
which revealed

00:09:19.634 --> 00:09:22.701
the hottest
food-ordering trends of 2022.

00:09:22.701 --> 00:09:23.968
And the trends
were pretty interesting.

00:09:23.968 --> 00:09:25.701
For example,
more people requested

00:09:25.701 --> 00:09:27.701
celery juice on Wednesdays.

00:09:27.701 --> 00:09:31.534
-Oh. Man, see, I always ordered
celery juice on Wednesday.

00:09:31.534 --> 00:09:35.300
-Yeah. On Friday, there's
a spike in cannoli orders.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.634
-Wow! I get cannolis, you know,
every Friday, too.

00:09:38.634 --> 00:09:40.300
That's crazy.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:43.734
-Yeah, well, apparently, orders
of ranch dressing went way down.

00:09:43.734 --> 00:09:47.067
-Ha! See, I didn't order
any ranch this year.

00:09:47.067 --> 00:09:49.000
[ Laughter ]

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:53.067
-And the big drink craze
was a negroni sbagliato.

00:09:53.067 --> 00:09:55.767
-Sbagliato, you say.
Those are good.

00:09:55.767 --> 00:09:57.467
The only thing better
is a margarita.

00:09:57.467 --> 00:09:59.234
It goes great with a steak.

00:09:59.234 --> 00:10:00.734
[ Laughter ]

00:10:00.734 --> 00:10:02.501
-It makes sense.
I mean, the most frequently

00:10:02.501 --> 00:10:06.501
paired food/drink combo
was steak and margarita.

00:10:06.501 --> 00:10:07.934
-Huh.
[ Ominous music plays ]

00:10:07.934 --> 00:10:10.133
Really?

00:10:10.133 --> 00:10:11.868
W-What about Saturdays?

00:10:11.868 --> 00:10:14.634
I got to be the only one
who orders tater tots

00:10:14.634 --> 00:10:17.734
and says to hold the --
-Sour cream.

00:10:17.734 --> 00:10:19.133
[ Laughter ]

00:10:19.133 --> 00:10:21.033
Dammit.
-W-What?

00:10:21.033 --> 00:10:22.467
What's wrong, Tariq?

00:10:22.467 --> 00:10:25.000
-No, it -- it can't be.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.934
-What?
W-- What is it?

00:10:26.934 --> 00:10:29.100
-No way, n-not me.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.000
-Say it.
What is it, Tariq?

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.133
[ Dramatic music crescendos ]

00:10:32.133 --> 00:10:34.067
-I think I might be
a basic bitch.

00:10:34.067 --> 00:10:35.200
[ Laughter ]

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:38.167
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:10:38.167 --> 00:10:41.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:41.734 --> 00:10:43.400
[ Laughs ]

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:47.934
[ Applause continues ]

00:10:47.934 --> 00:10:50.667
-Or you're a trendsetter.

00:10:50.667 --> 00:10:53.000
-Damn right I am!

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.367
-Whew!

00:10:54.367 --> 00:10:57.300
I was worried for a second.

