00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:08.000
a new reality dating show

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:09.367
called "MILF Manor."

00:22:09.367 --> 00:22:10.501
[ Laughter ]
-Ugh!

00:22:10.501 --> 00:22:12.634
-It features eight women,
eight younger men,

00:22:12.634 --> 00:22:15.434
and one shocking twist.

00:22:15.434 --> 00:22:16.701
Yeah, I think
the shocking twist is

00:22:16.701 --> 00:22:19.234
that TLC used to stand
for The Learning Channel.

00:22:19.234 --> 00:22:21.767
[ Laughter ]
-[ Claps ]

00:22:21.767 --> 00:22:24.100
-Actually, the shocking twist is
that it's hosted by Mike Pence.

00:22:24.100 --> 00:22:26.100
[ Laughter ]
-Really?

00:22:26.100 --> 00:22:28.634
-Well, I saw that
several TikTok users

00:22:28.634 --> 00:22:31.467
have been posting
their own Tinder Wrapped, okay?

00:22:31.467 --> 00:22:34.067
Where they wrap up
their year of dating.

00:22:34.067 --> 00:22:35.634
Yeah, and a lot of them
were very similar,

00:22:35.634 --> 00:22:37.801
so, since it's the holidays,
I'll sum them all up

00:22:37.801 --> 00:22:40.067
in the most festive way
possible. Here we go.

00:22:41.734 --> 00:22:43.334
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:22:43.334 --> 00:22:46.667
[ "The Twelve Days of Christmas"
plays ]

00:22:46.667 --> 00:22:48.734
[ Bells jingling ]

00:22:48.734 --> 00:22:51.434
♪ In the last day of Tinder ♪

00:22:51.434 --> 00:22:53.634
♪ My love life gave to me ♪

00:23:11.234 --> 00:23:13.501
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:23:15.100 --> 00:23:16.901
[ Laughter ]

00:23:18.434 --> 00:23:20.000
[ Laughter ]

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:25.300
-[ Joins in singing ]

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:26.300
What a year.

00:23:26.300 --> 00:23:27.634
♪♪

00:23:27.634 --> 00:23:28.801
Thank you very much.

00:23:28.801 --> 00:23:29.834
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:23:29.834 --> 00:23:32.534
Thank you very much.
Thanks, Steph.

00:23:32.534 --> 00:23:34.200
Guys, I read a new survey
that said

00:23:34.200 --> 00:23:38.033
the most stressful place to be
during the holidays is the mall.

00:23:38.033 --> 00:23:39.534
-Hm.
-It's so stressful,

00:23:39.534 --> 00:23:41.200
shoppers are walking
up to mall Santas like,

00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:42.200
"Let me get a swig of that."

00:23:42.200 --> 00:23:43.334
♪♪

00:23:43.334 --> 00:23:44.434
I'm in a great mood
because we're right

00:23:44.434 --> 00:23:45.868
in the middle
of the holiday season.

00:23:45.868 --> 00:23:47.634
Christmas is almost here.

00:23:47.634 --> 00:23:51.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:23:51.100 --> 00:23:53.634
And Hanukkah starts on Sunday.

00:23:53.634 --> 00:23:56.601
That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:23:56.601 --> 00:23:58.667
Hanukkah is celebrated
for eight nights,

00:23:58.667 --> 00:24:00.467
so the next time you complain
about your relatives

00:24:00.467 --> 00:24:02.234
at Christmas,
times that by eight.

00:24:02.234 --> 00:24:03.534
[ Laughter ]

00:24:03.534 --> 00:24:05.234
Of course, people are still
shopping for presents,

00:24:05.234 --> 00:24:06.534
and I heard that, this year,

00:24:06.534 --> 00:24:09.801
one of the most unwanted gifts
is beauty products.

00:24:09.801 --> 00:24:11.100
That makes sense.
You can't hand someone

00:24:11.100 --> 00:24:13.100
a bag of make-up like,
"I thought you needed this."

00:24:13.100 --> 00:24:15.067
[ Laughter ]

00:24:15.067 --> 00:24:17.167
Well, in a recent survey,
for the second year in a row,

00:24:17.167 --> 00:24:18.734
New Hampshire ranked
as the state

00:24:18.734 --> 00:24:20.968
with the most Christmas spirit.

00:24:20.968 --> 00:24:22.400
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:24:22.400 --> 00:24:24.300
Vermont was like,
"Excuse me.

00:24:24.300 --> 00:24:26.801
We have the
Ghost of Christmas Past.

00:24:26.801 --> 00:24:28.100
Hello."

00:24:28.100 --> 00:24:30.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:24:30.634 --> 00:24:31.767
I mean, come on.

00:24:31.767 --> 00:24:34.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:24:34.400 --> 00:24:35.534
Let's get to some news.

00:24:35.534 --> 00:24:37.501
Last night, several
high-profile journalists

00:24:37.501 --> 00:24:39.033
who have been covering Elon Musk

00:24:39.033 --> 00:24:41.501
had their
Twitter accounts suspended.

00:24:41.501 --> 00:24:43.934
Elon said the journalists
were using social media

00:24:43.934 --> 00:24:45.434
to keep track
of what he's doing,

00:24:45.434 --> 00:24:47.901
or as that's also known,
social media.

00:24:47.901 --> 00:24:50.133
[ Laughter ]

00:24:50.133 --> 00:24:51.601
I have a feeling that,
right after Christmas,

00:24:51.601 --> 00:24:54.367
we're gonna see Elon Musk in
line trying to return Twitter.

00:24:54.367 --> 00:24:56.501
[ Laughter ]

00:24:56.501 --> 00:24:58.467
It's a big weekend for sports,
'cause this Sunday

00:24:58.467 --> 00:25:03.667
is the World Cup final
between Argentina and France.

00:25:03.667 --> 00:25:05.267
Argentina and France.

00:25:05.267 --> 00:25:06.634
Of course,
my bracket's already busted.

00:25:06.634 --> 00:25:08.501
I had England and Gonzaga
in the final.

00:25:08.501 --> 00:25:10.033
[ Laughter ]

00:25:10.033 --> 00:25:11.434
Yep, Argentina versus France.

00:25:11.434 --> 00:25:12.767
At first, I wasn't sure
what was at stake,

00:25:12.767 --> 00:25:13.834
but then someone told me

00:25:13.834 --> 00:25:15.334
it's like "Evita"
versus "Les Mis."

00:25:15.334 --> 00:25:16.701
And I was like, "Oh, I get it."

00:25:16.701 --> 00:25:17.901
[ Laughter ]

00:25:17.901 --> 00:25:20.400
The final will be played
on Sunday at 10:00 a.m.,

00:25:20.400 --> 00:25:22.367
so if you want to know
why soccer isn't more popular

00:25:22.367 --> 00:25:24.934
in America, there's your answer.
[ Laughter ]

00:25:24.934 --> 00:25:26.300
Well, everyone's
talking about this.

00:25:26.300 --> 00:25:29.100
13 years after the original,
"Avatar: The Way of Water"

00:25:29.100 --> 00:25:31.234
has finally hit theaters.

00:25:31.234 --> 00:25:33.968
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:25:33.968 --> 00:25:35.267
This is wild.

00:25:35.267 --> 00:25:38.033
The movie has a run time
of 3 hours and 12 minutes.

00:25:38.033 --> 00:25:39.200
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:25:39.200 --> 00:25:40.834
That's not a movie,
that's a flight.

00:25:40.834 --> 00:25:42.167
[ Laughter ]

00:25:42.167 --> 00:25:44.033
Even Hanukkah is like, "Whoa.
How long we doing this?"

00:25:44.033 --> 00:25:45.467
[ Laughter ]

00:25:45.467 --> 00:25:47.434
If this was on Netflix,
the "Are you still watching?"

00:25:47.434 --> 00:25:49.267
thing would pop up 48 times.
[ Laughter ]

00:25:49.267 --> 00:25:51.734
"Yeah, I'm still watching."

00:25:51.734 --> 00:25:53.200
I read that, this weekend,
screenings of

00:25:53.200 --> 00:25:54.801
"Avatar: The Way of Water"
are selling out

00:25:54.801 --> 00:25:57.400
all across the country,
especially at IMAX theaters.

00:25:57.400 --> 00:26:00.100
And I think I know why.
Check out this ad I just saw.

00:26:00.100 --> 00:26:03.467
-You've never seen anything like
the underwater world of Pandora.

00:26:03.467 --> 00:26:05.868
And in honor of
"Avatar: The Way of Water,"

00:26:05.868 --> 00:26:08.334
IMAX has something else
you've never seen before.

00:26:08.334 --> 00:26:10.234
Introducing FLYMAX,

00:26:10.234 --> 00:26:13.601
the first large-format urinal,
designed to handle your stream

00:26:13.601 --> 00:26:17.534
after a 44-ounce Icee
and a 3-hour movie about water.

00:26:17.534 --> 00:26:20.701
Just zip and let 'er rip
as a cascade of blue liquid

00:26:20.701 --> 00:26:23.400
take yours urine on
the adventure of a lifetime.

00:26:23.400 --> 00:26:24.567
-Whoo!

00:26:24.567 --> 00:26:26.467
FLYMAX, by IMAX.

00:26:26.467 --> 00:26:28.534
Putting the "Aaa" in "Avatar."

00:26:28.534 --> 00:26:29.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:26:29.767 --> 00:26:30.968
-Yeah, that makes sense.

00:26:30.968 --> 00:26:33.901
[ Applause ]

00:26:33.901 --> 00:26:36.334
Some business news --
for the next three days,

00:26:36.334 --> 00:26:39.968
Starbucks union members
